+# GreatDANE (Dane) tree notes
+
+## Bundle ID migration: org.mozilla.surf.pepecoin.greatdane -> surf.dogecoin.dane
+
+nowon approved this on 2026-10-27. Plan: /workspace/patches/dane-esr153head/BUNDLE-ID-MIGRATION-PLAN.md
+
+- **0051** (871ceac538): bundle ID is now surf.dogecoin.dane. Uses `--with-distribution-id=surf` in mozconfig and
+  mozconfig-x86_64, and `MOZ_MACBUNDLE_ID=dogecoin.dane` in browser/branding/greatdane/configure.sh.
+  toolkit/moz.configure puts the helpers under the new ID: surf.dogecoin.dane.{plugincontainer,gpu-helper,media-plugin-helper}
+  (the updater and channelprefs follow too). The GreatDANE app name, the profile folder, the greatdane.* prefs and
+  the MAR channel greatdane-esr don't change.
+- **0054** (64f1606a70): renames the updater's dmgInstallHelper to surf.dogecoin.dane.dmgInstallHelper
+  (its LaunchDaemon plist is /Library/LaunchDaemons/surf.dogecoin.dane.dmgInstallHelper.plist).
+
+### What changes for users moving from an old-ID build (e.g. 6c4bedb9)
+
+- **Kept:** the profile folder ~/Library/Application Support/GreatDANE (named after the app, not the bundle ID).
+  That keeps bookmarks, prefs, Dane's saved logins (key4.db/logins.json) and the chain node data.
+- **Lost (keyed on the bundle ID):** camera, mic and location permissions (TCC), which macOS asks for again;
+  the default-browser choice, which the user has to set again; the ~/Library/Preferences defaults domain;
+  and any Keychain items the old app ID created.
+- **No auto-update:** old builds can't update to the new ID (DisableAppUpdate, the aus5.mozilla.org URL and
+  Mozilla's stock MAR certs). Users reinstall from https://dogecoin.surf/dane/download/ by dragging the new app
+  over the old one. The greatdane.doge start page carries this note.
